y gorilla $t$ years after birth grows at a rate of $3{t}^{2}+15.$ If, at $t=1$ years old, the gorilla weighed $20$ pounds, how much will the gorilla weigh at $3$ years old?" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305971 1113 #uuid "65f31595-eae0-5d16-93f8-31fb7f4c123c" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305971 1145 "Let $s(t)=3{t}^{2}+15$ be the rate at which the weight of the gorilla is changing and let $S(T)$ be the weight of the gorilla $T$ years after birth. \n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nS(T)=S(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(T) & =S(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =20+{\\int }_{1}^{T}3{t}^{2}+15\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =20+({t}^{3}+15t){|}_{1}^{T} \\\\  & =20+({T}^{3}+15T)-({1}^{3}+15\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =20+{T}^{3}+15T-16 \\\\  & ={T}^{3}+15T+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the weight of the gorilla $T=3$ years after birth, we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nS(3)={3}^{3}+15\\cdot 3+4=76.\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305973 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305974 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305975 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305976 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305977 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1041 "selection" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305974 13194139534727 true] [17592186305972 1110 #uuid "e4aaa94f-e585-5030-b83f-e00cc349746c" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305973 1034 "66" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305973 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305973 1111 #uuid "1846340a-f094-5b83-97a0-f3ac25fc7ee0" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305974 1034 "76" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953