04511ec-52be-5371-a34e-373cb41383f8" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305984 1145 "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=1,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(1)={\\int }_{0}^{1}10{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2}{e}^{2t+1}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =5({e}^{2(1)+1}-{e}^{2(0)+1}) \\\\  & =5({e}^{3}-e).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305986 13194139534727 true] [17592186305985 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534727 true] [17592186305985 1041 "field-1" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305985 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305986 13194139534727 true] [17592186305985 1110 #uuid "15c32acc-8411-57aa-bf4c-1b9f705f6c4e" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305986 1034 "5e^3-5e" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305986 1111 #uuid "d72ef5ab-f7ac-5d9b-b6bc-4129c414e95b" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305987 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305988 13194139534727 true] [17592186305987 1089 "q-346555" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305987 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534727 true] [17592186305987 1100 "Calculate $F\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ where $F(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}4{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$\n\n$F\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305987 1113 #uuid "253241dd-52ed-52fc-88ad-d3918465a0e8" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305987 1145 "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305989 13194139534727 true] [17592186305988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305990 13194139534727 true] [17592186305988 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534727 true] [17592186305988 1041 "field-1" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305988 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305989 13194139534727 true] [17592186305988 1110 #uuid "d12f264d-3ba4-5d07-b040-b7466bb9ce84" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305989 1034 "4" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305989 1111 #uuid "7a1ff148-3e6a-5111-84da-4c4ed26d0f68" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305990 1034 "0" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305990 1111 #uuid "594e318c-686f-50a4-9059-3f3a6e541f38" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305991 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305992 13194139534727 true] [17592186305991 1089 "q-346571" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305991 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534727 true] [17592186305991 1100 "Thermal energy is being added to a device at a rate of $3t$ joules per second. If at time $t=0$ the device already contains $15$ joules of energy, write an expression for $E(t),$ the total energy in the device at time $t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds.\n\n$E(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305991 1113 #uuid "4a02ce0b-fcf5-537f-9e67-1e008d4dbc2c" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305991 1145 "Let $f(t)=3t$ represent the rate at which energy enters the device, and let $E(T)$ be the total energy in the device after $T$ seconds.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nE(T)=E(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(T) & =E(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =15+{\\int }_{0}^{T}3t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={15+(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =15+\\frac{3{T}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable  $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nE(t)=15+\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305993 13194139534727 true] [17592186305992 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534727 true] [17592186305992 1041 "field-1" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305992 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305993 13194139534727 true] [17592186305992 1110 #uuid "6d5ec317-c86e-516a-a600-bba4f7067c61" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305993 1034 "15+\\frac{3}{2}t^2" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305993 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305993 1111 #uuid "15e3c40c-6dd5-54ac-9da9-191b271414e8" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305994 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305995 13194139534727 true] [17592186305994 1089 "q-346580" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305994 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534727 true] [17592186305994 1100 "In $2010$, a group of biologists started tracking the population of wolves in a mountain reserve. The initial population was $250,$ and the birth and death rates are given by $6+2t$ and $2+0.5t,$ respectively, where $t$ is the number of years since $2010.$  \n\nFind an expression for the population $P(t)$ of wolves in the reserve at any time $t>0.$\n\n$P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305994 1113 #uuid "9296910b-1e10-5a6e-946e-6ace46181e87" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305994 1145 "Let $p(t)$ be the rate of change of the population. According to the given information,\n\n$$\np(t)={{6+2t}_{⏟}}_{\\text{population increase}}-{{(2+0.5t)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{population decrease}}=4+1.5t.\n$$\n\nLet $P(T)$ represent the population of wolves $T$ years after $2010.$ By the accumulation of change formula, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)=P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T) & =P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =250+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(4+1.5t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =250+(4t+\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =250+4T+\\frac{3}{4}{T}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable  $t.$ We get \n\n$$\nP(t)=250+\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}+4t.\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305995 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305996 13194139534727 true] [17592186305995 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534727 true] [17592186305995 1041 "field-1" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305995 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305996 13194139534727 true] [17592186305995 1110 #uuid "348d0af4-b554-5d1b-b108-66ffbcb3f4b4" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305996 1034 "250+4t+\\frac{3}{4}t^2" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305996 1111 #uuid "08cb67e9-a358-5faf-ab35-30f2db224bc7" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305997 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305998 13194139534727 true] [17592186305997 1089 "q-49220" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305997 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534727 true] [17592186305997 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040150/assets/e0fc07ac8466381b668877e25cd0c9d8d5258a9061548e7b8efb12f75f6a0f04.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a quarter-circle of radius $2.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(3).$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305997 1113 #uuid "358026c7-0281-5a08-b21e-c3e38d8526e3" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305997 1145 "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040150/assets/923b60ed63551bda207f7e3eeb09e62f8b8eb7465a488858bef54bc36ab20baa.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-2,1],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a rectangle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [1,3],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a quarter-circle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-2,1],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the rectangle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [1,3],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the quarter-circle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3)={\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=6+\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305999 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306000 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306001 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306002 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306003 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1041 "selection" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306000 13194139534727 true] [17592186305998 1110 #uuid "17d607bb-eab4-51c5-bd28-49c8d0f4c11d" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305999 1034 "\\frac{6+\\pi }{2}" 13194139534727 true] [17592186305999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186305999 1111 #uuid "d0aa268c-325a-583c-9ba7-0b3d9e89dbc4" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306000 1034 "6+\\pi " 13194139534727 true] [17592186306000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186306000 1111 #uuid "17e8967b-bca2-5ead-bd67-e3a605574f3f" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306001 1034 "4+2\\pi " 13194139534727 true] [17592186306001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186306001 1111 #uuid "cd01c205-d891-541a-9c26-db04fe997332" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306002 1034 "\\frac{8+\\pi }{4}" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186306002 1111 #uuid "cdbee9a5-9083-5d57-8b27-888f5f2b78a7" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306003 1034 "5+2\\pi " 13194139534727 true] [17592186306003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186306003 1111 #uuid "ff31466e-2715-58b5-8a54-80bcd839e815" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306004 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306005 13194139534727 true] [17592186306004 1089 "q-49307" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306004 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534727 true] [17592186306004 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040150/assets/edcecf885aaf18a3aa6f6726c0485b1885e37132e73c8964de2576f7da5d61bf.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a quarter-circle of radius $2.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-3}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(0).$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306004 1113 #uuid "bf4d266f-0a91-53b9-91c1-64b2378d6063" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306004 1145 "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=0,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(0)={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040150/assets/bc8905f82a9f7525d6c59df337138e9f3b0417a45bc40f4b76fee2ddedac2eab.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-3,-2],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a square. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [-2,0],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a quarter-circle cut out of a rectangle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(0)={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-3,-2],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the square as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [-2,0],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the quarter-circle cut out of the rectangle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =bh-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =6-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(0)={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=1+(6-\\pi )=7-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306006 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306007 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306008 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306009 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306010 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1041 "selection" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306009 13194139534727 true] [17592186306005 1110 #uuid "a343680e-35d0-5efd-acb6-a8619246c610" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306006 1034 "6-\\pi " 13194139534727 true] [17592186306006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534727 true] [17592186306006 1111 #uuid "89a5ad42-9dca-58fb-9a9a-e8012c27d0ae" 13194139534727 true] [17592186306007 1034 "6+\\pi " 13194139534727 true] [17592186306007 1103 #